{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/run/current-system/sw/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' .ralph/projects/tank-sim/loops/007-tui-mvp-scenario-integration-and-full-regression/20260315070048-spec.md\"","aggregated_output":"---\nartifact: spec\nloop: 7\nproject: tank-sim\nbackend: claude(opus)\nrole: planner\ncreated_at: 2026-03-15T07:00:48Z\n---\n\n# Feature: TUI MVP, Scenario Integration, and Full Regression Suite\n\n## Description\nImplement the terminal user interface (Milestone 7) as a playable binary that lets users choose a scenario, run the simulation forward, perform all player actions, and observe chemistry/biology/events across five screens. Wire the TUI to consume `TankSnapshot` and dispatch `PlayerAction` via the `SimulationEngine` trait—never mutating state directly. Add a `tank_tui` binary entry point that integrates `tank_scenarios` for game setup. Strengthen the acceptance test suite to fully meet the 10 mandatory test specifications (in particular: extend `determinism_same_seed` to 720 hours with an action schedule, and extend `overfeeding_effects` to assert on detritus and nightly minimum DO, not only algae nuisance).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Running `cargo run -p tank_tui` launches an interactive terminal application\n- [ ] On startup, the user can select from the three preset scenarios (`nano_cycle`, `medium_planted`, `warm_room`) and choose a tank size / fill height\n- [ ] **Overview screen** displays: day/hour, temperature, pH, DO, TAN, NH3, nitrite, nitrate, plant status summary, shrimp status summary, and active warnings\n- [ ] **Chemistry screen** displays detailed chemistry values (all derived display values: GH, KH, TDS, conductivity, phosphate, DIC) and recent per-tick trend indicators (arrows or sparklines) for at least pH, TAN, DO, and temperature\n- [ ] **Biology screen** displays: plant guild biomasses and health, algae/periphyton biomass and nuisance index, shrimp counts (adults/juveniles/berried), condition/molt-stress/reproductive-readiness indices, biofilter maturity summary (AOB/NOB/comammox biomass or maturity proxy), and a microfauna summary\n- [ ] **Actions screen** provides input forms for all 12 `PlayerAction` variants: Feed, WaterChangePercent (with source profile selection), TrimPlants, SiphonDetritus, CleanFilter, AddShrimp, RemoveShrimp, ChangePhotoperiod, ChangeLightIntensity, ChangeHeaterSetpoint, ChangeAmbientTemperature, ChangeAeration\n- [ ] **Log screen** displays chronological event list from `TankSnapshot.recent_events` with severity coloring (Info=dim, Warning=yellow, Critical=red) and cause codes\n- [ ] Keyboard controls: Tab/number keys to switch screens; `h` to step 1 hour, `d` to step 1 day, `w` to step 1 week; space to toggle pause/auto-advance; `s` to save, `l` to load; `q` to quit\n- [ ] Auto-advance mode steps 1 hour per render tick (roughly 100–200ms interval) and can be paused/resumed with space bar\n- [ ] Save writes a JSON save file (via `tank_core` serialization) to a user-visible path; load restores from that file and resumes deterministically\n- [ ] The TUI only reads `TankSnapshot` for display and dispatches `PlayerAction` through `SimulationEngine::apply_action`—it never directly mutates `TankState` fields\n- [ ] Validation errors from `apply_action` are displayed as transient status messages in the UI, not panics\n- [ ] `determinism_same_seed` acceptance test runs 720 hours with a non-trivial action schedule (feed, water change, ambient temperature change) and asserts serialized snapshot identity\n- [ ] `overfeeding_effects` acceptance test compares control vs. overfed tanks for 14 days and asserts: (a) overfed has higher detritus, (b) overfed has lower nightly minimum DO, (c) overfed has higher algae nuisance index\n- [ ] All 10 mandatory acceptance tests pass under `cargo test --workspace`\n- [ ] `cargo clippy --workspace` and `cargo fmt --check` pass cleanly\n\n## Files to Modify/Create\n- `crates/tank_tui/Cargo.toml` — add dependencies: `tank_scenarios`, `tank_data`, `serde_json`, `anyhow` (for the binary); add `[[bin]]` section pointing to `main.rs`\n- `crates/tank_tui/src/main.rs` — **create** — binary entry point: terminal init, scenario selection menu, main event loop (input handling, simulation stepping, rendering), save/load dispatch, cleanup on exit\n- `crates/tank_tui/src/lib.rs` — expand `TuiApp` with: current `Engine` instance, auto-advance state, status message buffer, selected action form state, save file path; add methods for screen rendering dispatch and input routing\n- `crates/tank_tui/src/screens/mod.rs` — **create** — module declarations for screen renderers\n- `crates/tank_tui/src/screens/overview.rs` — **create** — Overview screen layout and rendering using `ratatui` widgets\n- `crates/tank_tui/src/screens/chemistry.rs` — **create** — Chemistry detail screen with trend indicators\n- `crates/tank_tui/src/screens/biology.rs` — **create** — Biology screen with plant, algae, shrimp, biofilter, microfauna summaries\n- `crates/tank_tui/src/screens/actions.rs` — **create** — Action input forms with field editing, validation feedback, and submission\n- `crates/tank_tui/src/screens/log.rs` — **create** — Event log screen with severity coloring\n- `crates/tank_tui/src/input.rs` — **create** — Keyboard input handling and dispatch (screen switching, stepping, action form interaction)\n- `crates/tank_core/tests/determinism.rs` — strengthen `determinism_same_seed` to 720 hours with action schedule\n- `crates/tank_core/tests/overfeeding_effects.rs` — **create** — dedicated overfeeding_effects test asserting detritus, nightly minimum DO, and algae nuisance comparisons over 14 days\n\n## Dependencies\n- Requires: Loop 6 (Shrimp Population Dynamics) — all simulation systems must be complete\n- Requires: `tank_scenarios` crate for scenario materialization (`seeded_state`, `default_scenario_ids`)\n- Requires: `tank_core` save/load serialization (already implemented)\n- Blocks: none (this is the final milestone)\n\n---\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
